1583
00:58:37.703 --> 00:58:41.100
and be like, that's a non-negotiable piece.

1584
00:58:41.100 --> 00:58:44.081
And I was really negotiating too much of myself away

1585
00:58:44.081 --> 00:58:46.383
when I was a lawyer, but I didn't realize it at the time.

1586
00:58:46.383 --> 00:58:49.073
And I think people are living at sort of like,

1587
00:58:50.220 --> 00:58:52.804
I think there's this pervasive, like malaise,

1588
00:58:52.804 --> 00:58:54.678
like people are living at like a 50%

1589
00:58:54.678 --> 00:58:56.390
and they're just okay with it.

1590
00:58:56.390 --> 00:58:57.844
Like, okay, isn't okay.

1591
00:58:57.844 --> 00:59:02.780
Like, you can actually be happy with the choices

1592
00:59:02.780 --> 00:59:05.590
that you make and the life that you're leading

1593
00:59:05.590 --> 00:59:08.720
if you evaluate what's really important to you.

1594
00:59:08.720 --> 00:59:10.345
Like, what are your triggers?

1595
00:59:10.345 --> 00:59:11.553
What's your passion?

1596
00:59:11.553 --> 00:59:15.959
And I'm really fortunate that running unlocked that for me.

1597
00:59:15.959 --> 00:59:19.468
But, you know, people do ask me all the time,

1598
00:59:19.468 --> 00:59:22.810
like how do I find that for me?

1599
00:59:22.810 --> 00:59:24.575
And I think it's not,

1600
00:59:24.575 --> 00:59:27.600
things that you're excited about that's not accidental.

1601
00:59:27.600 --> 00:59:31.130
Like, figure out a way to marry your skillset

1602
00:59:31.130 --> 00:59:34.020
with that thing that like makes you wanna wake up every day,

1603
00:59:34.020 --> 00:59:36.050
even if you were doing it for free.

1604
00:59:36.050 --> 00:59:38.584
And like really I would be doing the work I do now for free,

1605
00:59:38.584 --> 00:59:40.790
if I could, if I could afford it.

1606
00:59:40.790 --> 00:59:42.081
You know?

1607
00:59:42.081 --> 00:59:46.091
And I think that that's the stuff, like that's life.

1608
00:59:46.091 --> 00:59:48.800
Right, I mean, I think it's like a,

1609
00:59:48.800 --> 00:59:49.823
well, first of all,

1610
00:59:50.690 --> 00:59:52.719
you know, we're all just plugged into a certain way of life.

1611
00:59:52.719 --> 00:59:55.157
You know, it's like we're on this treadmill

1612
00:59:55.157 --> 00:59:58.317
of like the way that things are supposed to be.

1613
00:59:58.317 --> 01:00:00.248
And so we're not really compelled, you know,

1614
01:00:00.248 --> 01:00:02.600
we're not really encouraged I guess I should say

1615
01:00:02.600 --> 01:00:04.850
to look within at all really.

1616
01:00:04.850 --> 01:00:07.221
It's not really part of the Western culture of prerogative.

1617
01:00:07.221 --> 01:00:08.450
So, there's that.

1618
01:00:08.450 --> 01:00:11.818
And then we're all trying to fit in, like you said,

1619
01:00:11.818 --> 01:00:15.530
so that doesn't encourage individuality or staying weird

1620
01:00:15.530 --> 01:00:17.210
or kind of expressing what's authentic

1621
01:00:17.210 --> 01:00:18.373
and unique to yourself.

1622
01:00:18.373 --> 01:00:21.680
We're kind of, you know, programmed to do the opposite,

1623
01:00:21.680 --> 01:00:23.270
which is to repress that.

1624
01:00:23.270 --> 01:00:26.453
And so, after years and years and years of doing that,

1625
01:00:26.453 --> 01:00:29.040
it's almost flip for somebody to say,

1626
01:00:29.040 --> 01:00:29.963
well, like live your passion.

1627
01:00:29.963 --> 01:00:31.421
It's like most people are walking around,

1628
01:00:31.421 --> 01:00:34.345
like they're so disconnected from who they are,

1629
01:00:34.345 --> 01:00:37.404
that you can't even begin to answer that question.

1630
01:00:37.404 --> 01:00:39.894
Like, that question comes much later.

1631
01:00:39.894 --> 01:00:43.853
You know, there has to be a first step in

1632
01:00:43.853 --> 01:00:46.840
at least trying to develop a better relationship

1633
01:00:46.840 --> 01:00:49.380
