01:05:32.460 --> 01:05:33.740
but I haven't gotten to the point

1751
01:05:33.740 --> 01:05:35.350
where I'm doing it at night yet.

1752
01:05:35.350 --> 01:05:38.648
But I mean, I can definitely, it's made a huge impact on me.

1753
01:05:38.648 --> 01:05:41.420
And in the past, I'll do it for a while and I'll stop

1754
01:05:41.420 --> 01:05:42.253
and I'll do it for a while.

1755
01:05:42.253 --> 01:05:43.580
And I've been really thinking a lot about like,

1756
01:05:43.580 --> 01:05:44.797
why do I go in and out of it?

1757
01:05:44.797 --> 01:05:47.066
And what are the impediments to just creating

1758
01:05:47.066 --> 01:05:49.405
that kind of momentum and consistency?

1759
01:05:49.405 --> 01:05:50.624
I don't know that I have the answer to that,

1760
01:05:50.624 --> 01:05:53.250
but all I know is that it is working really well right now.

1761
01:05:53.250 --> 01:05:54.700
So, I'm getting more and more into it

1762
01:05:54.700 --> 01:05:56.750
and interested in hearing more about it.

1763
01:05:56.750 --> 01:05:58.300
But it was great to hear Dan's perspective

1764
01:05:58.300 --> 01:06:00.740
as being somebody who is such a skeptic, you know,

1765
01:06:00.740 --> 01:06:02.620
just really just, you know,

1766
01:06:02.620 --> 01:06:04.121
